I turn on the stove and heat a pan.
I pour some coconut oil into the pan.
First, I add the chopped onions into the hot oil.
I sauté the onions well.
It slowly turns a golden colour.
Then, I add the chopped tomatoes.
The recipe says, "Stir the tomatoes until soft."
I stir it well for five minutes.
After that, it is time to add the spices.
I add exactly two spoons of masala powder.
The kitchen fills with a wonderful smell.
Finally, I drop in the chicken pieces.
The recipe says, "Mix the meat well with the masala."
I stir everything together carefully.
Next, I pour in half a cup of water.
"Add enough salt and cover the pan," I read aloud.
I add salt and cover the pan.
Now the curry needs to simmer for twenty minutes.
